o for a flush in Characters (W), since there are several W tiles. Current W tiles: W1, W3, W4x2, W8x2, W9. That's 7 tiles. If I can collect more Ws, maybe aim for Full Flush (24 points) or Pure Straight (16 points) if I can get 1-9 in sequences.\n\nBut looking at the W tiles: W1, W3, W4, W4, W8, W8, W9. To make a Pure Straight (123, 456, 789), need W2, W5, W6, W7. Currently missing W2, W5, W6, W7. But maybe possible.\n\nAlternatively, maybe work on sequences in other suits. The B4-B5-B6 is already a Chow, so that's good. Then T7-T8 could become a Chow with T6 or T9.\n\nBut considering the valid actions, I need to discard one tile. Which discard keeps the most potential?\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nValid actions: Play T7, B5, W4, W9, J1, W3, W8, B4, B6, W1, T8, F4.\n\nLet's evaluate each:\n\n- Discard T7: Would leave T8. Maybe trying to keep T8 for a possible 789 if T9 comes, but T7 is part of a potential 678 or 789. But with only T7 and T8, discarding T7 leaves single T8.\n\n- Discard B5: B4, B5, B6 is a Chow. If I discard B5, breaks the Chow. But since it's concealed, maybe better to keep it. Unless I'm going for something else.\n\n- Discard W4: Have two W4s. Breaking the pair. Maybe risky, but if trying to build sequences instead.\n\n- Discard W9: Part of possible 789 in W (if W7 and W8 exist). But we have W8x2 and W9, so keeping W9 makes sense for that.\n\n- Discard J1: Honor tile. Not part of any sequence. Could be a candidate since honors are harder to use unless building All Honors or specific patterns.\n\n- Discard W3: Could be part of 123 or 345. With W1 and W3, maybe need W2 for 123. If W2 is available...\n\n- Discard W8: Have two W8s. Pair here. If aiming for 789, keeping W8 and W9 is good. Discarding one W8 would leave a single W8.\n\n- Discard B4 or B6: Breaks the B4-B5-B6 sequence. Probably not ideal.\n\n- Discard W1: Part of possible 123. With W1, W3, need W2.\n\n- Discard T8: Similar to T7; leaving T7.\n\n- Discard F4: Seat wind (North), which is wo